# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Panel deployment configuration.
# `make secrets` (setup/01-secrets.sh) copies this to .env and fills in the
# __*__ placeholders. Edit the REPLACE_ME values yourself.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# NameSilo API key: Domain Manager → API → generate key.
# Used by two things: Traefik (wildcard cert via DNS-01) and panel-ddns
# (creates + keeps current the apex A record for pietrasik.top; *.pietrasik.top
# is a one-time manual CNAME → apex, which ddns never touches).
NAMESILO_API_KEY=REPLACE_ME

# NameSilo TTLs are slow; keep the long propagation timeout.
NAMESILO_PROPAGATION_TIMEOUT=30m

# Let's Encrypt account email (expiry/abuse notices) — pre-filled; change if
# you want the notices in a different inbox.
ACME_EMAIL=connorgpietrasik@gmail.com

# Let's Encrypt ACME directory. FIRST bring-up runs against STAGING (no
# meaningful rate limits while you debug the NameSilo DNS-01 challenge; certs
# from staging are untrusted — browsers warn, which is expected). Once the
# staging cert has issued, `make deploy` promotes to production automatically:
# it stops traefik, wipes the ACME store (the staging account URI does not
# exist on prod — reusing it fails JWS verification), flips the config and
# restarts. Manual/idempotent fallback: make promote.
#   staging: https://acme-staging-v02.api.letsencrypt.org/directory
#   prod:    https://acme-v02.api.letsencrypt.org/directory
ACME_CA_SERVER=https://acme-staging-v02.api.letsencrypt.org/directory

# How long `make deploy` waits for the staging cert before giving up and
# leaving the promotion to a later `make promote` / `make deploy`. NameSilo
# DNS-01 propagation is the slow part (minutes, not seconds). 0 = don't wait.
#ACME_STAGING_WAIT=600

# How long the promotion step then waits for the PRODUCTION cert (warn-only
# on timeout — traefik keeps retrying on its own).
#ACME_PROMOTE_WAIT=300

# Shared secret Traefik injects as X-Panel-Token on /api requests.
# The host API rejects anything else. Never shown to clients.
PANEL_TOKEN=__PANEL_TOKEN__

# Filesystems the panel Overview shows disk dials for (comma-separated).
# Every entry always shows up: stats, or a loud ERROR on the dashboard —
# if it's listed here, you expect it to be there (statvfs on an unmounted
# mountpoint would otherwise silently show the containing filesystem).
PANEL_DISK_MOUNTS=/,/home,/models

# LLM servers: one shared API key for all of them (OpenAI-style bearer auth).
# Access policy is uniform — a key authorizes LLM use, not a specific server —
# so one value keeps client configs simple. Generate with:
#   openssl rand -hex 32   (prefix with sk- if you like)
# The LLM compose blocks fail fast at deploy time if it is unset. Split into
# per-server keys only if access ever varies by server; per-person keys =
# repeat --api-key (RUNBOOK → Add an LLM server).
#LLM_API_KEY=sk-REPLACE_ME

# Authelia secrets (generated). Rotate → change here + `docker compose up -d --force-recreate authelia`.
# session.secret
AUTHELIA_SESSION_SECRET=__AUTHELIA_SESSION_SECRET__
# storage.encryption_key (encrypts the sqlite TOTP/identity store — back this up!)
AUTHELIA_STORAGE_ENCRYPTION_KEY=__AUTHELIA_STORAGE_ENCRYPTION_KEY__
# identity_validation.reset_password.jwt_secret
AUTHELIA_JWT_SECRET=__AUTHELIA_JWT_SECRET__
